  "body": {
    "id": "thm:finite-design-regret",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Conditional on a supplied sound interval oracle and the certificate returned by Theorem \\(\\mathrm{oracle\\mbox{-}conditional\\mbox{-}capacity\\mbox{-}certificate}\\), uniformly for \\(p\\in\\mathcal P\\), the certified offset satisfies\n\\[\n J_N(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)-\\inf_{|\\gamma|\\leq G}J_N(p,\\gamma)\n \\leq\\epsilon+o(1).\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "JN",
      "p",
      "Pbox",
      "gammaepsilon",
      "gamma",
      "G",
      "epsilon"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:rate-bounds",
      "ass:rate-membership",
      "ass:staffing-window",
      "ass:staffing-cost-positive",
      "ass:information-cost-positive",
      "ass:test-size",
      "def:design-objective",
      "def:interval-oracle",
      "def:certificate-algorithm",
      "def:capacity-certificate",
      "thm:diffusion-poisson",
      "thm:certified-capacity-design",
      "thm:oracle-conditional-capacity-certificate"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Set\n\\[\n S_N(p,\\gamma)=V_{0,N}(p)+V_{1,N}(p,\\gamma),\n \\qquad\n S(p,\\gamma)=V_0(p)+V_\\gamma(p).\n\\]\nAll four summands are nonnegative because, by their definitions, they are stationary Poisson energies.  The uniform energy convergence in Theorem \\(\\mathrm{diffusion\\mbox{-}poisson}\\), whose compact domain is supplied by the rate-membership and staffing-window assumptions, gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n r_N\n &:=\\sup_{p\\in\\mathcal P,\\,|\\gamma|\\leq G}\n       |S_N(p,\\gamma)-S(p,\\gamma)|\\\\\n &\\leq\n \\sup_{p\\in\\mathcal P}|V_{0,N}(p)-V_0(p)|\n +\\sup_{p\\in\\mathcal P,\\,|\\gamma|\\leq G}\n       |V_{1,N}(p,\\gamma)-V_\\gamma(p)|\n \\longrightarrow0 .                                           \\tag{1}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nFor all \\(x,y\\geq0\\),\n\\[\n |\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}|^2\n =\\frac{|x-y|^2}{(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})^2}\n \\leq |x-y|,                                                   \\tag{2}\n\\]\nwhere the case \\(x=y=0\\) follows directly.  By the definitions of \\(J_N\\) and the capacity--precision objective \\(J\\), their staffing terms \\(c_M\\gamma\\) cancel.  Consequently, (1)--(2) imply\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n \\Delta_N\n &:=\\sup_{p\\in\\mathcal P,\\,|\\gamma|\\leq G}\n       |J_N(p,\\gamma)-J(p,\\gamma)|\\\\\n &\\leq c_I z_\\alpha\\sqrt{r_N}\n \\longrightarrow0 .                                           \\tag{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe multiplier in (3) is finite and positive: \\(c_I>0\\) by the information-cost assumption, while \\(\\alpha\\in(0,1)\\) implies \\(1-\\alpha/2\\in(1/2,1)\\), so \\(z_\\alpha=\\Phi^{-1}(1-\\alpha/2)\\in(0,\\infty)\\).  Thus (3) is uniform over the entire rate and staffing domain.\n\nFix \\(p\\in\\mathcal P\\) and write\n\\[\n \\mu(p)=\\inf_{|\\gamma|\\leq G}J(p,\\gamma).\n\\]\nUnder the supplied input name, sound interval oracle, and returned certificate appearing in the theorem's conditional premise, Theorem \\(\\mathrm{oracle\\mbox{-}conditional\\mbox{-}capacity\\mbox{-}certificate}\\) applies to the definitions of the interval oracle, certificate algorithm, and capacity certificate.  It yields\n\\[\n L_\\epsilon\\leq\\mu(p)\n \\leq J(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)\n \\leq U_\\epsilon,\n \\qquad\n U_\\epsilon-L_\\epsilon\\leq\\epsilon .                          \\tag{4}\n\\]\nIn particular,\n\\[\n J(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)-\\mu(p)\n \\leq U_\\epsilon-L_\\epsilon\n \\leq\\epsilon .                                                \\tag{5}\n\\]\nThe uniform comparison (3) also gives\n\\[\n \\inf_{|\\gamma|\\leq G}J_N(p,\\gamma)\n \\geq \\inf_{|\\gamma|\\leq G}\\{J(p,\\gamma)-\\Delta_N\\}\n =\\mu(p)-\\Delta_N,                                             \\tag{6}\n\\]\nand, because the certificate guarantees \\(\\gamma_\\epsilon\\in[-G,G]\\),\n\\[\n J_N(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)\n \\leq J(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)+\\Delta_N.                           \\tag{7}\n\\]\nSubtracting (6) from (7) and applying (5) proves\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n J_N(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)\n -\\inf_{|\\gamma|\\leq G}J_N(p,\\gamma)\n &\\leq J(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)-\\mu(p)+2\\Delta_N\\\\\n &\\leq\\epsilon+2\\Delta_N.                                    \\tag{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe number \\(\\Delta_N\\) does not depend on the selected \\(p\\), and (3) gives \\(2\\Delta_N=o(1)\\).  Taking the supremum over \\(p\\in\\mathcal P\\) in (8) therefore proves the claimed uniform \\(\\epsilon+o(1)\\) finite-system regret bound.  Every use of \\(\\gamma_\\epsilon\\) remains conditional on the supplied sound oracle and its certificate; hence the argument makes no unconditional model-specific oracle or staffing claim.",
    "justification": "Uniform diffusion-energy convergence transfers the limiting-objective certificate, now supplied by the constructed model-specific oracle, to the finite integer-capacity system.",
    "gap": "The asymptotic transfer retains its stated \\(o(1)\\) approximation term; the oracle-construction gap is discharged by Theorem \\(\\mathrm{certified\\mbox{-}capacity\\mbox{-}design}\\).",
    "consumer": "Combining the constructed oracle, the generic branch-and-bound certificate, and this transfer gives the staffing manager a checkable \\(\\epsilon+o(1)\\) finite-system regret guarantee.",
